{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He went up to Timnah.</b> For him the going was an ascent, for through it he begot two righteous men. But regarding Samson it is written וירד שמשון תמנתה, because the going was for him a descent, since through the woman he took there his eyes were gouged out." "<b>To shear his sheep.</b> She chose for herself that hour, when Judah was happy, for joy gives one the upper hand over his inclination, for they were accustomed to make a feast at the time of shearing sheep. And if you ask: how did HaKadosh Baruch Hu consent that all the kings of Judah should descend from the offspring that came from Tamar, who conceived through harlotry? One may answer: better that they descend from Tamar, daughter of Shem the righteous, than from the wife of Judah, who was a Canaanite woman, for they would have been flawed. And further, she did not conceive through harlotry, for before the giving of Torah all close relatives would perform levirate marriage, even the father of the deceased, and since Shelah did not levire her, it fell upon Judah to levire her. And when Torah was given, a halakhah was newly established not to levire except a brother from the father. Even so, if there are no brothers, they would levire with legitimate close relatives. And therefore she did what she did with permissibility, just as Boaz did with Ruth, even after the giving of Torah."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:56.095257090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}